// LIBERTASIAN — EAS App Store metadata-as-code (Apple only).
//
// REQUIRES, before running `eas metadata push`:
//   1. App registered in App Store Connect with bundle id `com.libertasian.app`
//      (see SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md → "Apple — register the app").
//   2. Credentials in place: `appleId`, `appleTeamId`, and `ascAppId` filled in
//      `eas.json` → `submit.production.ios` (currently `YOUR_*` placeholders).
//   3. Demo reviewer account created (MFA disabled) and the `apple.review` block
//      added below by hand — kept out of version control to avoid leaking the
//      demo credentials. See SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md → "Apple — review test account".
//
// Play Store has no EAS metadata-as-code equivalent — see `store/PLAY_LISTING.md`
// for the paste-ready Play Console copy.
//
// JSONC: leading `//` line comments are stripped by EAS' JSON5-tolerant parser
// (same convention used in `eas.json`). The CI JSON-validity check strips
// these comments before `JSON.parse` (see PR description for the one-liner).
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STATE OF THE LIVE LISTING - read before touching `description` or pushing.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// 1. 1.0.1 IS LIVE (Ready for Distribution). The live App Store description
//    is therefore the copy this file carried into that submission, and the
//    "...AI-generated ALAC answers for paid users" line App Review flagged
//    under Guideline 2.1(b) is retired. This file is where ASC copy is
//    written and copied FROM, so it must describe what we intend to submit
//    next - not what is live today, and not an aspirational corpus.
//
// 2. Two claims in `description` were FALSE and were corrected for 1.0.2
//    (2026-09-12), both measured against prod:
//      - Past Bar Exams said "from 1953-2024". The corpus holds 97 sittings
//        and 1,536 questions across only 13 distinct years between 2006 and
//        2022 (nothing from 2019-2021). Now reads "from 2006-2022".
//      - Codal Reader said "Republic Acts", plural. The corpus holds exactly
//        one (the Revised Corporation Code). The bullet now names the codes
//        actually shipped: Civil Code, Revised Penal Code, Labor Code,
//        Family Code, Tax Code, the 1987 Constitution, Rules of Court.
//    Apple FREEZES Description once a version is Ready for Distribution, so
//    neither correction reaches the store until a 1.0.2 submission carries
//    it. Overclaiming corpus coverage is the same metadata-vs-binary
//    mismatch that got builds 29 and 30 rejected - do not reintroduce it.
//
// 3. `eas metadata:push` has STILL never been run against this listing, and
//    must NOT be run. A push sends this file as the WHOLE listing:
//      - no `apple.review` block is committed (the demo reviewer credentials
//        are deliberately kept out of version control), so a push would
//        CLEAR the demo-account Sign-In fields already entered in App Store
//        Connect - the exact fields the reviewer needs to get past login.
//      - the `advisory` age-rating block below is commented out because
//        eas-cli rejects the legacy schema it uses. The age rating is
//        answered by hand in the ASC questionnaire; a push does not carry it.
//    Every field in App Store Connect goes in BY HAND, including this
//    description and the release notes below.
//
// 4. The Subscriptions paragraph and the three link lines at the end of
//    `description` are a REJECTION FIX, not decoration. App Review rejected
//    iOS 1.0.1 (build 29) under Guideline 3.1.2 on 2026-09-02 (submission
//    fa02a61a-b2c3-44d1-ac95-4409dfac3227) because the App Store product
//    page carried no functional Terms of Use (EULA) link. 3.1.2 requires the
//    product page itself to state the subscription terms and link a EULA;
//    the in-app Terms screen does not satisfy it. Apple exposes a dedicated
//    EULA field only for a CUSTOM agreement, so the standard EULA has to be
//    linked from the Description - which is why these lines live here and
//    must NOT be trimmed for length. `Terms of Use (EULA)` points at Apple's
//    standard EULA; `Service terms` points at ours, which is an addition to
//    it, not a replacement. No price appears in this copy on purpose: prices
//    are shown in the app before purchase, and hardcoding them here would
//    go stale per-storefront.
//
//    This text is applied to App Store Connect BY HAND (2026-09-02).
//    Do not run `eas metadata:push` to apply it - see item 3: a push would
//    clear the demo-account Sign-In fields the reviewer needs.
{
  "configVersion": 0,
  "apple": {
    "version": "1.0.2",
    "copyright": "2026 LIBERTASIAN Inc.",
    "categories": ["REFERENCE", "EDUCATION"],
    "info": {
      "en-US": {
        "title": "LIBERTASIAN",
        "subtitle": "Philippine legal research",
        "description": "LIBERTASIAN is a Philippine legal research library for law students, bar reviewees, and practitioners.\n\n• Past Bar Exams — 97 sittings, 1,500+ questions from 2006–2022 with AI-generated ALAC answers.\n• Case Digests — Philippine Supreme Court cases with facts, issues, ruling, doctrine, and provenance, generated from authoritative sources only.\n• Codal Reader — the Civil Code, Revised Penal Code, Labor Code, Family Code, Tax Code, the 1987 Constitution, and the Rules of Court, organized by bar subject with cross-references.\n• AI Study Assistant — chat and Q&A grounded in what you are reading. Sourced answers only; the model abstains rather than fabricate.\n• Camera Scan-to-Digest — point your camera at a pleading or case printout and get a structured digest with citations back to the source.\n• Offline codal cache and cross-device sync between mobile and web.\n\nPrivate by default. Your uploads, scans, and notes stay scoped to your organization. Nothing you upload is ever used to train our models or shared without your explicit consent.\n\nLIBERTASIAN provides AI-powered legal research tools for informational purposes only. AI outputs are not legal advice and do not create an attorney-client relationship. Always consult a qualified Philippine lawyer for legal matters.\n\nSubscriptions\nLIBERTASIAN Pro and LIBERTASIAN Edu are offered as monthly or annual auto-renewable subscriptions. The price of each option is shown in the app before you subscribe. Payment is charged to your Apple Account at confirmation of purchase. Your subscription renews automatically unless auto-renew is turned off at least 24 hours before the end of the current period, and your account is charged for renewal within 24 hours of the end of that period. You can manage your subscription or turn off auto-renew in your Apple Account settings after purchase.\n\nTerms of Use (EULA): https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/\nService terms: https://libertasian.com/terms\nPrivacy Policy: https://libertasian.com/privacy",
        "keywords": [
          "Philippine law",
          "bar exam",
          "case digests",
          "codals",
          "Supreme Court",
          "jurisprudence",
          "RA",
          "RPC",
          "law school"
        ],
        "releaseNotes": "\u2022 Case digests now keep loading as you scroll, instead of stopping after the first page.\n\u2022 Filter case digests by bar subject, with a live count for each subject.\n\u2022 Clearer free-tier limits throughout, and fixes to account switching.",
        "promoText": "Plain-language Philippine case digests, codals, and 1,500+ bar exam questions — built for Filipino law students and lawyers.",
        "marketingUrl": "https://libertasian.com",
        "supportUrl": "https://libertasian.com/contact",
        "privacyPolicyUrl": "https://libertasian.com/privacy"
      }
    },
